{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 35, :comments ["<b>And when [a man's ox] injures.</b> Ben Zuta said that רעהו [his fellow] is an attribute of the ox, but he did not see that שור איש [a man's ox] is the construct state, and likewise שור רעהו [his fellow's ox], and an ox has no fellow — only Ben Zuta alone. And this ox, which is תם [innocent], its owner shall pay half damages:"], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:37:13.592526052Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}